# Integer square root, digit by digit. Answers root, then r, then remainder.
#
#   rw progs/binsqrt.rw '<1001>'   ->   11r0      (sqrt 9 = 3, nothing over)
#   rw progs/binsqrt.rw '<1010>'   ->   11r1      (sqrt 10 = 3, 1 over)
#
# Same shape as bindiv.rw -- compare, then subtract if it fits -- but what you
# compare against is different every step. Taking two bits of the input at a
# time, the trial value is root*4+1 and the root gains a bit each round, so
# the thing being subtracted grows as the answer does.
#
# The identity that makes it tractable: root*4+1 written in binary is just the
# root's bits followed by 01. So the trial value and the root are the same
# region of tape, and a round updates it by inserting the new root bit in
# front of that trailing 01 -- one rule, no arithmetic:
#
#   fits    01^m -> 101^        root gains a 1
#   misses  01^n -> 001^        root gains a 0
#
# At the end the root is that region with its trailing 01 taken off again.
#
#   [ root 01 ^ | remainder = $ input >
#
# Pairs are counted from the low end, so an input of odd length needs a
# leading 0 first. e and o walk it to find out which, and p carries the pad
# back if it was odd.

# bootstrap: < is consumed, so this fires exactly once. The trial starts at
# 01, which is a root of nothing and a trial value of 1.
<->[01^|=$e

# is the input an odd number of bits? e means even so far, o means odd
e0->0o
e1->1o
o0->0e
o1->1e
e>->>
o>->p>
0p->p0
1p->p1
$p->$0

# a traveller on its way right, one at a time
T0->0T
T1->1T
T|->|T
U0->0U
U1->1U
U|->|U

# compare column: the digit is written back unchanged
0T%->%0
1T%->%1
0U%->&0
1U%->%1
0T&->&0
1T&->%1
0U&->&0
1U&->&1
|T%->|%
|U%->|&
|T&->|&
|U&->|&

# subtract column: same arithmetic, digit replaced
0T:->:0
1T:->:1
0U:->!1
1U:->:0
0T!->!1
1T!->:0
0U!->!0
1U!->!1
|T:->|:
|U:->|!
|T!->|!
|U!->|!

# @ walks the trial value leftwards, putting each bit back as it goes
0@->@0T
1@->@1U
[@->[H

# trial value spent: ripple the last borrow through the rest of the remainder
0&->&0
1&->%1
|&->|l
0!->!1
1!->:0
|!->|:

# the trial pointer walks home
H0->0H
H1->1H
H|->^|

# F goes back to wake it for a pass
0F->F0
1F->F1
|F->F|
^F->@

# n and m carry the decided root bit back, and the root grows in place
0n->n0
1n->n1
|n->n|
01^n->001^
0m->m0
1m->m1
|m->m|
01^m->101^

# it did not fit: park idle, the root gains a 0
l0->0l
l1->1l
l$->n=$

# it did fit and has been subtracted: park idle, the root gains a 1
:0->0:
:1->1:
:$->m=$

# it did fit: park in subtract mode and run the walk again
%0->0%
%1->1%
%$->F:$

# next two input bits. Last, as always.
=$00->F00%$
=$01->F01%$
=$10->F10%$
=$11->F11%$

# input spent: take the trailing 01 back off the root and tidy up. This has
# to consume the ^ as it fires -- a root that itself ends in 01 would match
# the rule a second time, and the root would be eaten a pair of bits at a time.
01^->R
[00->[0
[01->[1
[->
|00->|0
|01->|1
R|->r
=$>->
